# Gotchas only

This is systematic pattern detection and contradiction spotting with evidence
fraud analysis. It is not argument synthesis. Do not assemble a party's case,
pair competing recitals as impeachment, or write advocacy.

Incoming files are **scans of paper** (flatbed / print-then-scan / NYSCEF), not
native-born originals. Prefer content that survives OCR. Ordinary scan texture,
mixed page size, OCR noise, e-filing packaging, file-creation metadata, and
generic font mismatch are not case interrupts.

A gotcha is a claim checked against real evidence (sworn, documentary, or an
entered court act) that passes all four: same nameable fact, evidence runs
AGAINST the claim, material to an element/procedure/credibility/damages, and
both quotes are in the pulled text. Two motions or a claim vs a proposed order
is advocacy, not a gotcha. A model pass without those four completed steps does
not ship. When a pair is ambiguous, suppress it.

Related documents that show a defect about the same subject often SUPPORT a
denial. That is not a gotcha. Shared topic, person, or caption is not the same
fact. Evidence that restates the claim (not settled / case not settled; I live
at X / a record lists X) is FOR, not against.

He-said-she-said is not a gotcha. A denial versus the other side's competing
recital (including a bare service denial versus an affidavit of service, or a
service-attempt claim versus a DMV/address printout that lists or supports the
same address) is the ordinary dispute. The gotcha is when that party produces
evidence and that evidence is fraudulent or false — their exhibit undercuts the
claim, or the fraud/forensic check flags the exhibit they offered. Bought
bank/utility/invoice templates filled in, printed, and scanned are exhibit
fraud to look for. Court filings are out of scope for that check.

## Case-impact allowlist (interrupt)

Ship only when the finding hits at least one bucket:

- **Element** — e.g. personal jurisdiction / service, standing, default
- **Procedure / foundation** — authority to act, entered court act, same-CRFN
  discharge vs continued reliance
- **Credibility** — party's own exhibit is false or internally impossible
- **Damages** — fee/amount that is not ordinary loan-status movement

Primary exhibit-fraud signals (content that survives a scan): impossible
statement dates, consumer-statement math that does not reconcile, leftover
template chrome, historical impossibility on the exhibit body. Secondary only
with statement context: strong localized overlay/ELA on a consumer statement —
never whole-page scan texture alone, never on pleadings/deeds as a standalone
interrupt.

Case-level structural interrupts stay sparse: same-CRFN discharge vs continued
reliance, conflicting first-default/notice/foreclosure dates (not same-month
noise), fee conflicts that are not amortization.

## Suppress (do not interrupt)

Note rate versus default/penalty rate, remaining principal, and the installment
amount that change after missed payments or amortization are expected
loan-status movement — ignore them. Recorded public instruments (mortgages,
deeds, assignments) are not bank statements; do not treat rounding or loan-math
quirks as findings unless there is a genuine alteration signal.

Also suppress: caption/party list; NYSCEF header; filing-stamp vs body date;
arrears demand letters citing older installments; shared index/caption year
only; jurat-only “edited exhibit” cards; OCR garbage quotes; font/spelling
nuance; metadata or editor-software alone; scan-heavy ELA without a content
hook; mixed page size/rotation/AcroForm on court filings; exhibit letter or
number label mismatches (labels routinely change between initial filing and
the recorded packet — “Referenced Exhibit A is not in this case” is not an
interrupt).

Do not hardcode practice-area phrases. Types are only: factual contradiction,
chronology inconsistency, material omission, procedural/foundational, admission
against interest.

Risk scores from verified findings only — never document type or title.
